e disease name **SpecificDisease**, even when a post-nominal participial phrase (e.g., \"[verb-ing] [noun]\") or other modifying material follows.\n  - A parenthetical abbreviation that defines or restates a SpecificDisease head **inherits SpecificDisease** from its antecedent. It must not inherit the label of a larger span that contains it.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do **not** apply this rule when the disease string is a non-referential attributive label fused into a noun phrase whose head denotes a non-disease entity (e.g., a population, case set, gene, protein, phenotype, or family-history record). In that case, label the string **Modifier**. The rule also does not cover generic common-noun uses of \"disease\" that do not name a specific condition, or cases where the disease name is hyphen-fused into a compound premodifier of a non-disease head.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1956, "output_tokens": 2171, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1763}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}